ow list: it enumerates the repo and asserts on the SHAPE of what survives. Suite 33/33, mutation sweep **15/15 killed**, restore verified. Three more bugs surfaced by running rather than reading — `lstrip("./")` eating the leading dot off `.agents/` paths (this repo's **third** time, silently switching off half of `merge_eligible` while green), `section()` reading shell comments as markdown headings, and an unreachable root guard the sweep proved dead. ⭐ **Then R4 DELETED it.** Three operator constraints — not per machine, do not change the agent's own rules, must work for all four platforms — and R3's Part C-2 (allow-list lines in the **gitignored** `settings.local.json`) failed all three, taking the agent-self-merge split with it. So the road is now: `gh pr create` → **the operator clicks Merge** → `--after-merge` verifies with plain git. `land_pr.py` (470 lines), its 69 tests, the sweep, the prose predicate that took four cuts to get right, and BOTH doors' `## Break-glass` sections are gone. The break-glass road could never have worked anyway: measured against its own contents it needs github.com + Actions + `gh` + a token + a checkout on `main` — a strict **superset** of the PR door, so no outage exists in which it helps. Everything the deleted script checked is already held by an existing gate or a server setting (table in the walkthrough). Suite 32/32, lint 0/0, maps clean; **zero** permission surfaces touched. Owed: two server-side settings that cover both machines and all four platforms at once. | [plan](2026-08-16_direct-main-fastlane/implementation_plan.md) · [walkthrough](2026-08-16_direct-main-fastlane/walkthrough.md) · task.yaml + gates/ receipt |
